  About shopkeepers:

  Shopkeepers are human, right?  So why not make them a little bit
more human, by letting them have armor, rings, amulets, weapons etc.
just like the player?  They could still have more attacks/strength/you
name it to make robbing shops at least somewhat difficult, but imagine
the following scenario:

  You enter a shop.
  "Hello player, welcome to Rath Luirc's general store!"
  You pick up some items, time passes, until you happen to be next to a
large mimic:
  "You feel an incredible urge to hit the wand next to you! --More--"
  "You miss the large mimic. The large mimic hits! You die... --More--"

  Obviously, the shopkeeper was wearing a ring of conflict...
  Or similarly, if the shopkeeper is wearing a ring of hunger, you
might see him go and eat every % in the shop one by one, or a ring of
teleportation might have him jumping all around the shop, a ring of polymorph
would change him into a grey dragon/demilich/whatever from time to time...

  The same goes for different types of armor; zap the shopkeeper with a
wand of lightning and witness the beam bounce off his shield of reflection
and so on...  The possibilities are endless.
